speechtext:
Madam Speaker, in the absence of the Minister of Indian Affairs and Northern Development, my question is directed to the Prime Minister. On October 31, 1978, the government signed an agreement with the Committee for Original Peoples Entitlement to settle Inuvialuit land claims. In the January 16, 1981, edition of News of the North, the Minister of Indian Affairs and Northern Development is quoted as having stated in a letter of December 24 to the federal government's chief negotiator that;
-some parts of the agreement-in-principle, signed between the Committee for Original Peoples Entitlement (COPE) and the government, are not acceptable to cabinet and must be changed before a final agreement can be reached.
It seems that this government intends to repeat-

The
contract was awarded by the Department of Supply and Services on behalf of the Department of National Defence.
(a)	The field service representative provides the following support services:
serves as a technical consultant to the Director of Aeronautical Engineering Maintenance (DAEM) at National Defence Headquarters (NDHQ); assists in evaluating technical publications, correspondence and messages;
affords rapid liaison between the contractor, Canadair Limited and DAEM/NDHQ on technical problems, flight safety matters, special investigations and fields queries;
assists logistics cells and specialist personnel at NDHQ on technical problems arising out of operation and maintenance of the aircraft and aircraft
systems;
assists in supply matters by identification of equipment and spares;
assists DAEM staff in reviewing technical correspondence exchanged as a result of the tripartite agreement to determine CF-116 (CF-5) applicability;
receives, collates and maintains for quick reference all technical information emanating from the contractor or field FSRs relating to the CF-116 (CF-5) aircraft.
(b)	The period of time covered by the contract is April 1, 1980, to March 31, 1981.
February 2, 1981

(c)	The contracts are awarded annually on a continuing basis provided an approved requisition defining the services required is received from the Department of National Defence.
